            is
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle+categories"} tangent bundle categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            with a trivial (in the appropriate sense) tangent bundle is a cartesian differential category.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We present the revised definition of a cartesian differential category due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geoff+Cruttwell"} Geoff Cruttwell
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Cruttwell"} see below
          %p The adjective “cartesian” refers to the existence of finite products.
          %p
            A prototypical example of a carteisan differential category is the category whose objects are open subsets of finite-dimensional real vector (or affine) spaces and morphisms are smooth maps. Below, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subset R^n
            is such an object, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_0(U)=R^n
            is the tangent space at any point of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong (generalized) cartesian differential category
              is a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with finite products equipped with the following data:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for any object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
                  a commutative monoid
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mn 0
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(X)=(L_0(X),+_X\colon L_0(X)\times L_0(X)\to L_0(X),0_X\colon 1\to L_0(X))
                %p
                  (the tangent space at any point) such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(L_0(X))=L(X)
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(X\times Y)=L(X)\times L(Y)
              %li
                %p
                  for any morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(f):L_0(X)\times X \to L_0(Y)
                  (the derivative of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                              %mi X
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(+_X)=+_X\circ p_1
                      ,
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mn 0
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mn 0
                              %mi X
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(0_X)=0_X\circ p_1
                      (where
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
                      projects onto the first factor of a product);
                  %li
                    %p (the derivative is a linear map)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo +
                      %mi X
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo +
                      %mi X
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(f)\circ (a +_X b,c)=D(f)\circ (a,c) +_X D(f)\circ (b,c)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mn 0
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 0
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(f)(0_X,a)=0_X
            %p
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b,c\colon A\to L_0(X)
              are morphisms in
              = succeed ");" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %ul
